  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In amylose,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></math>glycosidic linkage is present.<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8b891569-75c4-4e17-bf04-e6983085be01-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 170px;\" /><br />So, this option statement is incorrect.</p><p>Sucrose has 1,2-glycosidic linkage between glucose and fructose.&nbsp;</p>cellulose and amylose has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></math>glycosidic linkage. lactose contains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>-</mo></math>galactose and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>-</mo></math>glucose. maltose and lactose has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></math>glycosidic linkage.",
